---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const relationships = [
  ["First before", "The earliest related activity before the cohort event."],
  ["Last before", "The most recent related activity before the cohort event."],
  ["First after", "The next related activity after the cohort event."],
  ["Last after", "The latest related activity after the cohort event."],
  ["First in between", "The first related activity before the cohort activity repeats."],
  ["Aggregate in before", "A count, sum, min, or max across related activities before the cohort."],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Temporal joins — Activity Schema"
  description="Learn how Activity Schema combines independent business events using customer and time instead of pre-modeled foreign-key relationships."
  path="/temporal-joins/"
>
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">The querying unit</p>
    <h1>Relate activities through time.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Temporal joins combine independent activities using an entity and timestamp. They let you describe the relationship you mean—<strong>last before</strong>, <strong>first after</strong>, or <strong>in between</strong>—at query time.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section-tight timeline-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="timeline-card card">
        <div class="question">
          <span class="mono">Question</span>
          <p>Which email did a customer open before completing an order?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline" role="img" aria-label="A timeline showing opened email as the last activity before completed order">
          <div class="axis" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="event muted first-event">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <code>started_session</code>
            <small>08:42</small>
          </div>
          <div class="event selected second-event">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <code>opened_email</code>
            <small>09:04</small>
            <b>last before</b>
          </div>
          <div class="event cohort third-event">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <code>completed_order</code>
            <small>09:41</small>
            <b>cohort</b>
          </div>
          <div class="event muted fourth-event">
            <span class="dot"></span>
            <code>opened_email</code>
            <small>10:08</small>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="query-plan mono">
          <span>for every</span><code>completed_order</code><span>append</span><code>last before opened_email</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A compact vocabulary</p>
        <h2>Ask for the relationship you actually mean.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The cohort activity is the grain of the result: one row for every completed order, support ticket, session, or other event you are investigating. Append activities add context around each cohort event.</p>
        <p>Because every activity uses the same entity-and-time structure, the shape of a temporal relationship can be reused. Change the activity names; keep the query pattern.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shell relationship-grid grid-3">
      {relationships.map(([name, description]) => (
        <article class="card">
          <span class="relation-mark mono">↔</span>
          <h3>{name}</h3>
          <p>{description}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section assemble-section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Build at query time</p>
        <h2>Assemble a useful table from small events.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A narrow activity stream can become a wide analysis table when you need it. Start with a cohort event, borrow features from related activities, and aggregate the history around each row.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shell assembly card">
      <div class="assembly-input">
        <span class="input-label">Cohort activity</span>
        <code>completed_order</code>
      </div>
      <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      <div class="assembly-input">
        <span class="input-label">First after</span>
        <code>shipped_order</code>
      </div>
      <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      <div class="assembly-input">
        <span class="input-label">Last before</span>
        <code>opened_email</code>
      </div>
      <span class="equals" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <div class="assembly-output">
        <span class="input-label">Analysis row</span>
        <code>order · ship time · campaign</code>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shell actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/ActivitySchema/ActivitySchema/blob/main/2.0.md#relationships">Read every relationship <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/ai/">See how AI can use this</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .timeline-section {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .timeline-card {
    padding: clamp(24px, 5vw, 48px);
  }

  .question span,
  .input-label {
    color: var(--steel);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .question p {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 12px 0 72px;
    color: var(--navy);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .timeline {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    min-width: 680px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    padding-block: 26px 34px;
  }

  .axis {
    position: absolute;
    top: 31px;
    right: 5%;
    left: 5%;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
  }

  .event {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .dot {
    z-index: 1;
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border: 3px solid var(--white);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--fog);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line);
  }

  .event code {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .event small {
    color: var(--fog);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
  }

  .event b {
    position: absolute;
    top: -24px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.58rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .event.selected .dot {
    background: var(--seafoam);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px rgba(68, 180, 139, 0.14);
  }

  .event.selected b {
    background: rgba(68, 180, 139, 0.12);
    color: var(--seafoam-dark);
  }

  .event.cohort .dot {
    background: var(--navy);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px rgba(17, 26, 74, 0.1);
  }

  .event.cohort b {
    background: rgba(17, 26, 74, 0.08);
    color: var(--navy);
  }

  .event.muted code {
    color: var(--fog);
  }

  .query-plan {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--midnight);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.48);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .query-plan code {
    color: var(--seafoam-light);
  }

  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 72px;
  }

  .relationship-grid {
    margin-top: 72px;
  }

  .relationship-grid article {
    min-height: 220px;
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .relation-mark {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    color: var(--seafoam-dark);
  }

  .relationship-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--steel);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .assemble-section {
    background: var(--white);
  }

  .assembly {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1.2fr;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 64px;
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .assembly-input,
  .assembly-output {
    display: grid;
    min-height: 106px;
    align-content: space-between;
    padding: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .assembly-output {
    border-color: var(--seafoam);
    background: rgba(68, 180, 139, 0.07);
  }

  .assembly code {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  .plus,
  .equals {
    align-self: center;
    color: var(--fog);
  }

  .timeline-card {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
    }

    .assembly {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .plus,
    .equals {
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }
</style>
